ine  that in reality if you were to try and  make this pipeline on your own  might take you maybe a few hours a few  days or even a few weeks depending on  your level of expertise but you'll see  how quick and simple this could be right  here  so first of all what we'll do is we'll  clean up those raw reads  and we'll make sure that we remove the  technical adapters  from library preparation we will then  address the  issue of pcr amplification that could  bring in some technical  variation that we don't want to confuse  with biological simple  signal then we will align these reads to  the reference genome using both type 2  and then we will quantify the levels of  expression  to get a table of fpm gene expression  using rsem once we've completed this  pipeline i can click on  end and i will take a look at some of  the output data  so it's a real quick process to go from  having that raw data to then analyzing  that data and you  saw some of the variations into the  pipeline that you can make as you go  through  and then get getting a result so that  you can appreciate the inputs and the  outputs very quickly  once you get those results importantly  we have  all kinds of additional methods to line  this data visualize this data  and even integrate multi-omics data to  quickly understand the relationship  between  gene expression genomic variants  maybe microrna and long non-coding rna  as well as some clinical information
 

